Hotel pick (within 20 km of MAN)
- Whitworth Locke (hotel_id: 3814760), city centre
  - Est. price for 3 nights: about £459 (subject to change)
  - Review score: 8.9 (Fabulous)
  - Style: Aparthotel (25 m² studio), kitchenettes; check-in from 16:00, checkout by 11:00
  - Location: ~14 km from the airport on Princess Street near Oxford Road (great for walking/trams)
  - Getting there from MAN:
    - Train: Airport → Manchester Piccadilly (~15–20 min), then 12–15 min walk or short tram/bus
    - Metrolink Tram: Airport → city (~45–50 min, change at Cornbrook if needed)
    - Taxi/ride-hail: ~20–35 min depending on traffic

Fun around Whitworth Locke (walkable)
- Manchester Art Gallery (~5–7 min)
- The Palace Theatre & Oxford Road Corridor food/drink (~2–5 min)
- Canal Street & the Gay Village (~7–10 min)
- St Peter’s Square & Central Library (~8–10 min)
- Science and Industry Museum, Castlefield (~15–20 min)
- John Rylands Library & Deansgate/Spinningfields (~12–15 min)
- Northern Quarter (street art, indie shops, bars) (~15–18 min)
- National Football Museum & Medieval Quarter (~20–25 min)
- Additional nearby landmark: St Mary’s Catholic Church (~0.4 km)

3-day sightseeing route
Day 1 (Sat, Nov 9) – Arrival and city intro
- 13:00 arrival → drop bags (check-in from 16:00; hotel can hold luggage)
- Afternoon: St Peter’s Square → Manchester Art Gallery → Chinatown coffee/snack
- Evening: Deansgate/Spinningfields OR Canal Street
  - Dinner: Mackie Mayor (food hall), Rudy’s Neapolitan Pizza (Peter St), or The Refuge (nearby)

Day 2 – Museums + football or street-art focus
- Morning: Science and Industry Museum (Castlefield); walk canals to Roman Fort
- Lunch: Castlefield/Deansgate (Dukes 92, Albert’s Schloss near Peter St)
- Afternoon (choose one):
  - Football: Old Trafford or Etihad Stadium tour (prebook; tours limited on match days)
  - Culture: John Rylands Library → Spinningfields → Chetham’s Library/Medieval Quarter
  - Street Art: Northern Quarter loop (Stevenson Sq → Tariff St → Thomas St)
- Evening: Northern Quarter bars (e.g., Cane & Grain, The Smithfield Social), cocktails at Schofield’s (book if possible)

Day 3 – Quays or green escape
- Option A: Salford Quays (Metrolink)
  - Imperial War Museum North → The Lowry → MediaCity & dockside walk
- Option B: Football deep-dive
  - National Football Museum → stadium tour you didn’t do on Day 2
- Option C: Easy countryside taster
  - Train to Marple/Edale (Peak District) for a short ridge or canal walk (weather-permitting)
- Farewell dinner back in town (Dishoom, El Gato Negro, or Hawksmoor Deansgate)

Practical tips
- Transport: Contactless works on Metrolink (daily caps). Trains are quicker to/from the airport.
- Weather in November: Cool and changeable—bring layers and a rain jacket; daylight fades ~4:30 pm.
- Book ahead: Stadium tours, John Rylands Library exhibits, and popular restaurants.
- Luggage timing: If you’d like earlier access, I can look for hotels with guaranteed early check-in.

Want more hotel options?
